# LitBank (dbamman/litbank): the source archive at the pinned commit,
# downloaded and hashed on 2026-10-28 (30,172,625 bytes). The README at
# the same commit states LitBank is licensed under a Creative Commons
# Attribution 4.0 International License and that the corpus is drawn from
# the public domain texts on Project Gutenberg, as samples of about 2,000
# words of each of 100 works of English-language fiction (210,532
# tokens); it was read on 2026-10-28 (SHA-256
# 10e740b0beb5482490c0dc4eabd0c79a31eb881fa895c18b49993cd9e31af268).
# The annotations live in the same tree as per-book brat files.
name: litbank
tier: default
url: https://github.com/dbamman/litbank/archive/3e50db0ffc033d7ccbb94f4d88f6b99210328ed8.zip
sha256: 0e881d887c167b2b196a3e887f88484a7ae64af2dda4ea5e41c660591f002cf6
license-url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dbamman/litbank/3e50db0ffc033d7ccbb94f4d88f6b99210328ed8/README.md
license: CC BY 4.0
note: The README grants CC BY 4.0 over the annotations; the text it annotates is public domain on Project Gutenberg, so no separate text terms are claimed here.
note: Attribution: David Bamman, Sejal Popat and Sheng Shen (NAACL 2019) for entities, Sims, Park and Bamman (ACL 2019) for events, and Bamman, Lewke and Mansoor (LREC 2020) for coreference.
note: LitBank was not in docs/licences.md before this recipe; the licence claim comes from the read above, not from the earlier table.
